WEBVTT

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:09.000
I'm working a broken toe cast on to end up
with a nice tubular edge for my ribbing.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.720
My needles are arranged for one by one
ribbing, and I'll start

00:00:14.786 --> 00:00:16.890
with a zigzag cast on.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.610
Both carriages are set for plain knitting.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.200
I'll hang the ribber cast on comb,
making sure the comb is hanging

00:00:24.266 --> 00:00:27.320
in the loops of the ribber needles.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:32.770
Next, I'll disengage the ribber carriage
the carriage from the main carriage,

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.530
pass it, and drop all the ribber loops.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.480
The cast on comb will be
hanging in those loops.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:47.640
I'll pass the carriage back and rejoin
the ribber and the main bed carriages.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:50.410
There are no changes to the carriages yet.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.770
I'll knit another zigzag row.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:58.770
Notice that the main bed now has stitches
and the ribber now has new loops.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.850
At this point, I'll hang
weights in my cast on comb.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:06.810
Next, I'll knit
the tubular rows with slip.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.960
I'll set the main bed to slip in one
direction and the ribber to slip

00:01:11.026 --> 00:01:12.930
in the opposite direction.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.250
In other words, I'm going to knit only
the ribber stitches first,

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:24.080
then knit only the main bed stitches,
then knit only the ribber stitches.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:31.730
I'll finish by canceling slip on both
carriages and set for plain knitting,

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:35.280
and then knit one row in ribbing.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.560
Following my pattern,
I'll continue knitting in ribbing.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.280
When the ribbing rows are complete,
I'll transfer the ribber

00:01:47.346 --> 00:01:50.320
stitches to the main bed.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.690
When all of the stitches are up
on the main bed, I can drop the ribber,

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.730
follow my pattern and continue knitting.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:06.960
Once the knitting is off the machine,
there's a strand of yarn passing

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:11.200
through the loops of that cast-on edge.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:15.370
Opposite the cut end of yarn that was used
for cast-on,

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:19.010
pull the strand and gather the edge.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:23.250
Hit this edge with a shot
of steam and set the stitches.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:27.560
This will eliminate any flare
and create a beautiful cast-on edge.

